# The bundle's own handover *template*. assemble-bundle re-emits it on every
# run, and the host's real handover is arsenal/session/handover.md — so a
# tracked copy here is a file nobody owns that dirties the tree before every
# worker loop. verify-subtree already excludes it for the same reason.
claude-arsenal/session/handover.md

# Candidate data — the most sensitive artefact in the system (spec §2).
# The profile store holds psychological dimensions and a story bank of
# failures; none of it belongs in a repository that may be shared.
profiles/

# Generated pipeline artefacts (offers, extractions, rankings).
data/
.claude/worktrees/

# T5's labelling aid (tools/labelling_page.py) — a build artefact of the
# corpus and the dimension model, regenerable at any time. The labeller's
# actual work lives in the browser's localStorage until exported and applied
# with `harness import`; this file itself carries no state worth committing.
corpus/labelled/label.html

